# gawk -- generated by tools/gen-recipes.sh, safe to edit.
# Source pins come from ../versions.env so a bump is one file.

SRC_URL=$GAWK_URL
SRC_SHA256=$GAWK_SHA256
SRC_DIR=$GAWK_SRCDIR

# --sysconfdir=/etc, AND GAWK IS THE ONE PACKAGE THAT PROVABLY NEEDED IT.
#
# extras/Makefile.am installs gawk.sh and gawk.csh into $(sysconfdir)/profile.d.
# The generic build.sh passes --prefix=/usr and nothing else, and autoconf --
# unlike meson, which special-cases a /usr prefix and maps sysconfdir to the
# absolute /etc -- defaults sysconfdir to ${prefix}/etc. So both files shipped
# to /usr/etc/profile.d.
#
# This is not a suspicion: a scan of every published payload in the index (615
# rows, both architectures, every subversion) found exactly one package with
# anything under usr/etc, and it was this one, in all four of its published
# rows. gnome-menus hit the identical mechanism and was caught by hand.
#
# tools/gen-recipes.sh now emits this flag for every recipe it generates, so a
# regenerated gawk would produce this same line; the flag is written here
# because the generator refuses to overwrite a recipe that already exists.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES IS THE ADDRESS, NOT THE READERSHIP. These two files define
# shell helper functions (gawkpath_prepend and friends) and set nothing by
# themselves, so nothing was breaking while they sat in /usr/etc -- the cost was
# dead weight in the payload, not a broken gawk. Whether anything sources
# /etc/profile.d at all is duct-filesystem's business, not this recipe's: its
# /etc/profile carried no loop over that directory until recently. That is a
# fact to re-check there, not a consequence to restate here.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-nls --sysconfdir=/etc"
